Modifications made in this product (summary; see README.md for details):
- Exclusive three-tier expert placement for Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (VRAM, RAM and
  SSD by share or count), runtime placement switching through
  /admin/expert-placement, and expert swapping within the placement's counts.
- A frame limit that holds every routed expert in VRAM.
- --served-model-name aliases.
- A prefix-cache tail snapshot for fresh one-call spans, in both resume modes
  (the finish endpoint covers continuations only; without the tap, repeats of
  a prompt that fits one call start from the root).
- A zero-token prefix-cache resume for exact repeats (every drafter mode;
  under MTP the drafter's pending cell is written by the resumed lane's
  first round): the prompt-end snapshot carries the pre-head residual, and the
  repeat regenerates its first token from it with no prefill (value-gated:
  skipped within one tap separation of the deepest published frontier, so
  only spans whose opener demoted to the last inner boundary capture).
- A construction-exact exact route for Qwen3.8-Flash-Next recipe C (BF16, INT8
  and FP8 KV): column-invariant dense, hyper-connection, QSA attention and MTP
  drafter routes and the recurrent GDN prefill at every width, so prefill
  splits, decode and verification give a position the same bits; prefix-cache
  resumes, taps and endpoints then run at any position without the
  free-cache-resume path. Recipe C's fast route runs the compensated chunked
  GDN prefill (gdn-compensated: every chunk product of high/low operand pairs,
  the recurrent arithmetic's error order at chunked speed).
- A Disk tier for the Qwen3.8-Flash-Next prefix cache (--prefix-cache-disk,
  --prefix-cache-disk-gib): KV blocks and state snapshots on the SSD through
  cuFile (GPUDirect Storage or its compatibility mode), sized apart from RAM,
  kept across restarts by a journal, spilled from the RAM tier or, with the
  RAM tier off, written through; it replaces this model's whole-file save.
- Batched DFlash2 drafting at any round size with an online cost fit.
- Prefill beside decode for Qwen3.8-Flash-Next: while another request decodes,
  prompt calls are split (--prefill-chunk-beside-decode) and each but the
  prompt's last runs inside the decode round's Forward (mixed rounds; bit for
  bit the separate calls on the construction-exact exact route).
- Tool-call grammar fixes: call openers inside Markdown code stay text under a
  constrained auto contract, and such a turn may end inside its thinking
  (non-strict calls there are recovered).
- Linux VRAM spill detection fix (no WDDM budget).
- A model-layer restructure: each family owns its instance construction, option branches
  and linear shape tuning under src/models/<family>/ (the shapes as extern tables the
  ops dispatch scans), the shared expert-offload tier lives in src/models/offload/
  (infernix_offload, parameterized by ExpertBankGeometry), and the Qwen frontend both
  families share lives in src/models/qwen_common/; the runtime engine keeps only
  family-neutral code (src/runtime/engine/engine_options.* holds the shared
  artifact-free checks and defaults, and the registry detects the artifact architecture).

